  "key_decisions": [
    "Talking animals (and the talking crowd of little animals and birds, plus the animal jurors) are photoreal CGI animals with only the period props the text gives them. The Gryphon and the Mock Turtle are photoreal CGI creatures. The Frog- and Fish-Footmen are CGI frog- and fish-bodied figures in livery; their anatomy is flagged for H2.",
    "SUP-004 is unchanged: card figures and human dream-figures stay human performers.",
    "The same photoreal-animal register is extended to non-speaking dream animals (puppy, hedgehogs, flamingoes, the pig-baby end-state). This is an interpretation and is flagged for H2.",
    "New WR-010 and XA-magic-08: the dream environments use the Art Nouveau / Mucha design language fully, built as photographed sets and set extensions. The waking frame gets at most a subtle influence. The 1862 lock still holds for costume, props and the waking world.",
    "Animal-bodied figures stay registered as CHAR-* (they are speaking characters). 04-creatures supplies their CGI anatomy.",
    "Corrected a long-standing misquote: the Bible said 'realistic drama', but brief.md reads 'Realistic fantasy film adapted from a fairy tale'.",
    "No downstream file was edited. Card-figure files that cite SUP-002 alongside SUP-004 were left alone, because the card rule is unchanged."
  ],
